  "faq.q1": "What is ATMOS Studio?",
  "faq.a1": "<strong class=\"text-white\">ATMOS Studio</strong> is an AI architectural visualization suite. It turns hand sketches, CAD drawings and massing models into professional imagery without leaving your computer.",
  "faq.q2": "Which workspaces does it include?",
  "faq.a2": "Three: <strong class=\"text-white\">floor plans</strong> with strict orthographic projection, aerial <strong class=\"text-white\">masterplans</strong> with roofs and site context, and <strong class=\"text-white\">3D perspectives</strong> — eye level, straight-on or aerial, indoors and outdoors.",
  "faq.q3": "Which representation techniques does it offer?",
  "faq.a3": "Four: <strong class=\"text-white\">editorial photorealism</strong>, monochrome <strong class=\"text-white\">clay maquette</strong>, <strong class=\"text-white\">architectural watercolour</strong> and <strong class=\"text-white\">ink sketch</strong>. In the three artistic ones the geometry is traced: the building is not redesigned.",
  "faq.q4": "Where are my drawings and renders stored?",
  "faq.a4": "Your privacy is absolute. Cloud processing is strictly ephemeral: your render is generated on secure servers, transmitted to your device, and the temporary file is automatically deleted from our infrastructure. Your projects and images are only permanently saved on your own device if you choose to tap 'Save'.",
  "faq.q5": "Which styles and materials does it include?",
  "faq.a5": "<strong class=\"text-white\">8 architectural styles</strong>, from Rustic to Wabi-Sabi, and <strong class=\"text-white\">47 materials</strong> with their own texture: woods, marbles, stones, concretes, ceramics and special surfaces.",
  "faq.q6": "Does it work with hand sketches?",
  "faq.a6": "Yes. It is built to read the human line: a photo of a napkin sketch, a quick iPad drawing or a technical plan. The clearer the drawing, the better the geometry is read.",
